{"agent_id":"pp3g-kA0n-final-patch-correctness-revision-of-the-154-durable","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-05T23:46:24.561094971Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e8d793ca-3c95-474b-ae98-609ffcbe254b","comment_uuid":"5441dfe5-b827-4950-945f-331c79a0a1e3","author":"pp3g-kA0n-final-patch-correctness-revision-of-the-154-durable","content":"# DESIGN (FINAL, round 3): Durable opencode silent-hang fix (#154) — IMPLEMENTATION-READY\n\n**Sub-issue**: #186 (round 3 of #180) · **Parent**: #154 · **Epic**: #156\n**Designer**: Builder pp3g-kA0n (design-only task; no code/binary changes made)\n**Inputs**: #180 (revised design, round 2); r1 verdict #182 (V1–V5, F-new-1..9); r3 verdict #184 (F5-1, F5-2, B1-1, B3-1, F5-3); #175 (baseline); #154; #144; #145; #179.\n**Verification basis**: all patch anchors and every claim below were re-derived THIS session against a real upstream checkout at `/tmp/opencode/opencode-upstream-r3` (`git describe` = v1.18.13, both files byte-identical to v1.18.12), effect `4.0.0-beta.83` at `/tmp/opencode/effect-check/package`, the live installed binary, live production config, and retained harness artifacts.\n\n**Verdict status**: round-3 revision. All five r1 blocking conditions (V1–V5), both r3 conditions (F5-1, F5-2), all three r3 minor findings (B1-1, B3-1, F5-3), and all nine r1 minor findings (F-new-1..9) are resolved below with **final, compilable patch hunks against the verified v1.18.13 source**, a **self-consistent verification matrix**, and a **change-log vs #180**.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Current state (unchanged from #180, re-confirmed)\n\n- Installed binary **1.18.13** (180,381,824 bytes), #179 byte-patch applied to **both** guard copies (`function dy` v1 + `function or` v2, `if(false)return` present 2×, original guard 0×), `\"autoupdate\": false` set.\n- Production config: `chunkTimeout=300000`, `headerTimeout=300000`, `timeout=3600000` on `opencode` and `opencode-go`; no `bodyIdleTimeout` yet.\n- This revision changes no files and no binaries; §6 \"step 0\" interim actions are implementation steps, not actions taken here.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Primary-source verification table (re-derived this session)\n\nEvery patch anchor used below was read from the v1.18.13 checkout; effect API claims were read from the fetched effect 4.0.0-beta.83 package. This table replaces trusting the #180 change-log.\n\n| Claim | Verified source | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `provider.ts` `wrapSSE` L37–82, guard L40; `timeoutController` starts L84 | `provider.ts` | ✔ |\n| `provider.ts` `resolveSDK` fetch wrapper L1736–1768; `chunkAbortCtl` explicitly named | `provider.ts` | ✔ |\n| `packages/core/src/aisdk.ts` (235 lines) `wrapSSE` L26–72, guard L29; `prepareOptions` L74–119; `signals.find(...)` at L95 returns **first** controller only | `aisdk.ts` | ✔ (V1 defect confirmed verbatim) |\n| `aiskd.ts` does not exist; the file is **`aisdk.ts`** | `ls packages/core/src/aisdk.ts` | ✔ (typo) |\n| `retry.ts` `policy()` L176–199; step = `Effect.succeed((meta) => …)`; non-retryable stop = `return Cause.done(meta.attempt)` (L185, synchronous); retry branch = `Effect.gen` (L186–197) | `retry.ts` | ✔ |\n| `Cause.done(value)` returns `Effect<never, Done<A>>` (fails in error channel); `Pull<A,E,Done,R> extends Effect<A, E \\| Cause.Done<Done>, R>` | effect `Cause.d.ts:1472`, `Pull.d.ts:36` | ✔ (Effect-aware `Cause.done` restructure typechecks) |\n| `meta.attempt` is a 1-based retry count; `delay(attempt) = 2000·2^(attempt−1)`, capped `RETRY_MAX_DELAY_NO_HEADERS=30s`, retry-after honored | `retry.ts` + upstream `retry.test.ts` | ✔ |\n| `APIError.metadata` = `Schema.Record(Schema.String, Schema.String)` ⇒ `metadata?.code` is `string \\| undefined`; `SessionV1.APIError.isInstance` name-check works on parsed errors | `core/src/v1/session.ts:61` | ✔ |\n| `ZlibError` → `APIError { isRetryable: true, metadata.code: \"ZlibError\" }` (unless aborted) | `message-v2.ts:638–651` | ✔ (F-new-1) |\n| `llm.ts` L7 imports `{ Context, Effect, Layer }` (no `Duration`); L371–377 `Stream.fromAsyncIterable(result.result.fullStream, …)` with no deadline; `cfg.experimental?.openTelemetry` pattern at L208/L345 | `llm.ts` | ✔ |\n| `Stream.timeoutFail` **does not exist**; `Stream.timeout` (L2966) silently ends; **`Stream.timeoutOrElse({ duration, orElse: () => Stream })` exists (L3042), documented \"The timeout is checked for each pull\"** (per-pull idle semantics) | effect `Stream.d.ts` | ✔ (F5-1) |\n| `Stream.fail` exists | effect `Stream.d.ts:789` | ✔ |\n| Config schemas: `core/src/v1/config/provider.ts` Struct L96–121 (`timeout`/`headerTimeout`/`chunkTimeout` + `Schema.Record(…, Schema.Any)` rest); `core/src/v1/config/config.ts` `experimental` Struct L169–185 (`mcp_timeout` etc.) | config sources | ✔ (F-new-3) |\n| bun gate in `packages/script/src/index.ts:5–18`, range `^1.3.14` (caret, from root `packageManager`), imported as `@opencode-ai/script`; `IS_PREVIEW = CHANNEL !== \"latest\"` at L31 | `script/src/index.ts` | ✔ (F-new-4, F-new-6) |\n| `cli/upgrade.ts:10` `if (config.autoupdate === false \\|\\| Flag.OPENCODE_DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE) return`; `getReleaseType` compares semver major/minor only | `upgrade.ts`, `installation/index.ts:24–36` | ✔ (F-new-6 inert under autoupdate:false) |\n| TUI notification exact-matches `data.message === \"SSE read timed out\"` | `tui/src/feature-plugins/system/notifications.ts:23` | ✔ (F-new-8) |\n| `packages/opencode/test/provider/header-timeout.test.ts` has `it.live(\"chunkTimeout raises a response stream error when SSE body stalls\")` with a live HTTP fixture — reusable template for `wrapBodyIdle` unit tests | upstream test | ✔ (F-new-9a) |\n| Harness: `cfg/opencode.json` has `chunkTimeout: 3000, headerTimeout: 2000, timeout: 15000`; runner `run-test.sh` wraps `opencode run` in shell-level `timeout \"$OUTER\" …` (GNU timeout; EXIT 124 = outer kill) | `/tmp/opencode-hang-test/cfg`, `/tmp/opencode-11813-verify/run-test.sh` | ✔ (V2, F5-3) |\n| Wrapper `~/.local/bin/opencode` already spawns `\"$REAL\" models` on every launch | wrapper | ✔ (F-new-7) |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Final patches — executable hunks against v1.18.13\n\n### 2.1 Patch A — `packages/opencode/src/provider/provider.ts` (v1)\n\n**Hunk A1 — insert `wrapBodyIdle` after `wrapSSE` (after L82, before `function timeoutController`):**\n\n```ts\n// NEW: idle-progress deadline for non-SSE response bodies (Option A').\n// The timer resets on every chunk, so a slow-but-progressing body is never\n// aborted (hy3 F2 preserved); only a body that stalls >= ms between chunks is.\n// Optional absoluteMs is a belt-and-braces total cap (opt-in, default off).\nfunction wrapBodyIdle(res: Response, ms: number, ctl: AbortController, absoluteMs?: number) {\n  if (typeof ms !== \"number\" || ms <= 0) return res\n  if (!res.body) return res\n  const reader = res.body.getReader()\n  let settled = false\n  let streamCtl: ReadableStreamDefaultController<Uint8Array> | undefined\n  let idleId: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined\n  let absoluteId: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined\n\n  // Shared failure path for the idle timer, the absolute-cap timer, and\n  // consumer cancel. Deterministically terminates the stream: errors the\n  // stream controller (so the consumer's read settles even if pull never\n  // ran), aborts the request controller, and clears BOTH timers.\n  const fail = (err: Error) => {\n    if (settled) return\n    settled = true\n    if (idleId) clearTimeout(idleId)\n    if (absoluteId) clearTimeout(absoluteId)\n    ctl.abort(err)\n    streamCtl?.error(err)\n    void reader.cancel(err).catch(() => {})\n  }\n\n  const body = new ReadableStream<Uint8Array>({\n    start(ctrl) {\n      // ReadableStream calls start synchronously at construction, so the\n      // absolute-cap timer (armed below) always has a controller to error.\n      streamCtl = ctrl\n    },\n    async pull(ctrl) {\n      if (settled) return\n      const part = await new Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<typeof reader.read>>>((resolve, reject) => {\n        idleId = setTimeout(() => {\n          const err = new ProviderError.ResponseStreamError(\"Body read timed out\")\n          fail(err)\n          reject(err)\n        }, ms)\n        reader.read().then(\n          (part) => {\n            if (idleId) clearTimeout(idleId)\n            idleId = undefined\n            resolve(part)\n          },\n          (err) => {\n            if (idleId) clearTimeout(idleId)\n            idleId = undefined\n            reject(err)\n          },\n        )\n      })\n      if (settled) return\n      if (part.done) {\n        settled = true\n        if (absoluteId) clearTimeout(absoluteId)\n        ctrl.close()\n        return\n      }\n      ctrl.enqueue(part.value)\n    },\n    async cancel(reason) {\n      fail(reason instanceof Error ? reason : new Error(String(reason)))\n    },\n  })\n\n  if (typeof absoluteMs === \"number\" && absoluteMs > 0) {\n    absoluteId = setTimeout(() => {\n      fail(new ProviderError.ResponseStreamError(\"Body read deadline exceeded\"))\n    }, absoluteMs)\n  }\n\n  const headers = new Headers(res.headers)\n  // fetch() has already decoded content-encoding into res.body and the\n  // re-chunked body no longer matches the original content-length. Keeping\n  // these headers makes consumers re-decode (double-decode -> ZlibError in\n  // the unbounded class) or wait on a stale length. Strip both.\n  headers.delete(\"content-length\")\n  headers.delete(\"content-encoding\")\n  return new Response(body, {\n    headers,\n    status: res.status,\n    statusText: res.statusText,\n  })\n}\n```\n\n**Lifecycle guarantees (closes F7/V3):** (1) the absolute-cap callback calls `fail`, which has the stream controller (captured in `start`) and calls `streamCtl?.error(err)` — the consumer's read settles deterministically even when the timer fires before the first `pull`; (2) the idle callback clears `absoluteId` via `fail` (no 55-min timer leak); (3) `cancel()` clears both timers via `fail` before any early-return; (4) `settled` prevents `ctrl.close()` after `ctrl.error()`; (5) `reader.cancel(...).catch(() => {})`; (6) `pull` early-returns once settled.\n\n**Hunk A2 — `resolveSDK` fetch wrapper (L1736–1768) — dispatcher:**\n\n```diff\n         const customFetch = options[\"fetch\"]\n         const chunkTimeout = options[\"chunkTimeout\"]\n         const headerTimeout = options[\"headerTimeout\"]\n+        const bodyIdleTimeout = options[\"bodyIdleTimeout\"]\n+        const bodyAbsoluteTimeout = options[\"bodyAbsoluteTimeout\"]\n         delete options[\"chunkTimeout\"]\n         delete options[\"headerTimeout\"]\n+        delete options[\"bodyIdleTimeout\"]\n+        delete options[\"bodyAbsoluteTimeout\"]\n\n         options[\"fetch\"] = async (input: any, init?: BunFetchRequestInit) => {\n           const fetchFn = customFetch ?? fetch\n           const opts = init ?? {}\n           const chunkAbortCtl = typeof chunkTimeout === \"number\" && chunkTimeout > 0 ? new AbortController() : undefined\n+          const bodyIdleAbortCtl =\n+            typeof bodyIdleTimeout === \"number\" && bodyIdleTimeout > 0 ? new AbortController() : undefined\n           const headerTimeoutMs = headerTimeout === false ? undefined : headerTimeout\n           const headerTimeoutCtl = typeof headerTimeoutMs === \"number\" ? timeoutController(headerTimeoutMs) : undefined\n           const signals: AbortSignal[] = []\n\n           if (opts.signal) signals.push(opts.signal)\n           if (chunkAbortCtl) signals.push(chunkAbortCtl.signal)\n+          if (bodyIdleAbortCtl) signals.push(bodyIdleAbortCtl.signal)\n           if (headerTimeoutCtl) signals.push(headerTimeoutCtl.signal)\n           if (options[\"timeout\"] !== undefined && options[\"timeout\"] !== null && options[\"timeout\"] !== false)\n             signals.push(AbortSignal.timeout(options[\"timeout\"]))\n\n           const combined = signals.length === 0 ? null : signals.length === 1 ? signals[0] : AbortSignal.any(signals)\n           if (combined) opts.signal = combined\n\n           const res = await fetchFn(input, {\n             ...opts,\n             // @ts-ignore see here: https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/16682\n             timeout: false,\n           }).finally(() => headerTimeoutCtl?.clear())\n\n-          if (!chunkAbortCtl) return res\n-          return wrapSSE(res, chunkTimeout, chunkAbortCtl)\n+          const isSSE = res.headers.get(\"content-type\")?.includes(\"text/event-stream\")\n+          if (isSSE) {\n+            if (!chunkAbortCtl) return res\n+            return wrapSSE(res, chunkTimeout, chunkAbortCtl)\n+          }\n+          if (!bodyIdleAbortCtl) return res\n+          return wrapBodyIdle(res, bodyIdleTimeout, bodyIdleAbortCtl, bodyAbsoluteTimeout)\n         }\n```\n\n### 2.2 Patch B — `packages/core/src/aisdk.ts` (v2) — V1 CLOSED\n\n> **Filename note (B1-2):** the file is `packages/core/src/aisdk.ts` (\"AI SDK\"). The #180 design wrote `aiskd.ts` in §2.1, §2.3, and — critically — the §6.5 mandatory rebase checklist. This revision uses `aisdk.ts` everywhere; the rebase checklist below (§6.5) is corrected.\n\n**Hunk B3 — insert `wrapBodyIdle` after `wrapSSE` (after L72, before `function prepareOptions`)** — identical structure to Hunk A1 with the file's existing plain-`Error` style (matches `new Error(\"SSE read timed out\")` at aisdk.ts L36):\n\n```ts\nfunction wrapBodyIdle(res: Response, ms: number, ctl: AbortController, absoluteMs?: number) {\n  if (typeof ms !== \"number\" || ms <= 0) return res\n  if (!res.body) return res\n  const reader = res.body.getReader()\n  let settled = false\n  let streamCtl: ReadableStreamDefaultController<Uint8Array> | undefined\n  let idleId: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined\n  let absoluteId: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined\n\n  const fail = (err: Error) => {\n    if (settled) return\n    settled = true\n    if (idleId) clearTimeout(idleId)\n    if (absoluteId) clearTimeout(absoluteId)\n    ctl.abort(err)\n    streamCtl?.error(err)\n    void reader.cancel(err).catch(() => {})\n  }\n\n  const body = new ReadableStream<Uint8Array>({\n    start(ctrl) {\n      streamCtl = ctrl\n    },\n    async pull(ctrl) {\n      if (settled) return\n      const part = await new Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<typeof reader.read>>>((resolve, reject) => {\n        idleId = setTimeout(() => {\n          const err = new Error(\"Body read timed out\")\n          fail(err)\n          reject(err)\n        }, ms)\n        reader.read().then(\n          (part) => {\n            if (idleId) clearTimeout(idleId)\n            idleId = undefined\n            resolve(part)\n          },\n          (err) => {\n            if (idleId) clearTimeout(idleId)\n            idleId = undefined\n            reject(err)\n          },\n        )\n      })\n      if (settled) return\n      if (part.done) {\n        settled = true\n        if (absoluteId) clearTimeout(absoluteId)\n        ctrl.close()\n        return\n      }\n      ctrl.enqueue(part.value)\n    },\n    async cancel(reason) {\n      fail(reason instanceof Error ? reason : new Error(String(reason)))\n    },\n  })\n\n  if (typeof absoluteMs === \"number\" && absoluteMs > 0) {\n    absoluteId = setTimeout(() => {\n      fail(new Error(\"Body read deadline exceeded\"))\n    }, absoluteMs)\n  }\n\n  const headers = new Headers(res.headers)\n  headers.delete(\"content-length\")\n  headers.delete(\"content-encoding\")\n  return new Response(body, {\n    headers,\n    status: res.status,\n    statusText: res.statusText,\n  })\n}\n```\n\n**Hunk B4 — `prepareOptions` fetch wrapper (L74–119) — FINAL COMPILABLE VERSION (V1 fixed):**\n\nThe two defects in #180's hunk 4 are both removed: `bodyIdleAbortCtl` is now **declared**, and controller selection no longer uses `signals.find(...)` (which returns only the first controller). Both controllers are named explicitly, mirroring hunk A2.\n\n```diff\n   const customFetch = options.fetch\n   const chunkTimeout = options.chunkTimeout\n+  const bodyIdleTimeout = options.bodyIdleTimeout\n+  const bodyAbsoluteTimeout = options.bodyAbsoluteTimeout\n   delete options.chunkTimeout\n+  delete options.bodyIdleTimeout\n+  delete options.bodyAbsoluteTimeout\n   options.fetch = async (input: Parameters<typeof fetch>[0], init?: RequestInit) => {\n     const opts = { ...(init ?? {}) }\n-    const signals = [\n-      opts.signal,\n-      typeof chunkTimeout === \"number\" && chunkTimeout > 0 ? new AbortController() : undefined,\n-      options.timeout !== undefined && options.timeout !== null && options.timeout !== false\n-        ? AbortSignal.timeout(options.timeout)\n-        : undefined,\n-    ].filter((item): item is AbortSignal | AbortController => Boolean(item))\n-    const chunkAbortCtl = signals.find((item): item is AbortController => item instanceof AbortController)\n-    const abortSignals = signals.map((item) => (item instanceof AbortController ? item.signal : item))\n+    const chunkAbortCtl = typeof chunkTimeout === \"number\" && chunkTimeout > 0 ? new AbortController() : undefined\n+    const bodyIdleAbortCtl =\n+      typeof bodyIdleTimeout === \"number\" && bodyIdleTimeout > 0 ? new AbortController() : undefined\n+    const abortSignals = [\n+      opts.signal,\n+      chunkAbortCtl ? chunkAbortCtl.signal : undefined,\n+      bodyIdleAbortCtl ? bodyIdleAbortCtl.signal : undefined,\n+      options.timeout !== undefined && options.timeout !== null && options.timeout !== false\n+        ? AbortSignal.timeout(options.timeout)\n+        : undefined,\n+    ].filter((item): item is AbortSignal => Boolean(item))\n     if (abortSignals.length === 1) opts.signal = abortSignals[0]\n     if (abortSignals.length > 1) opts.signal = AbortSignal.any(abortSignals)\n\n     if (\n       (pkg === \"@ai-sdk/openai\" || pkg === \"@ai-sdk/azure\" || pkg === \"@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock/mantle\") &&\n       opts.body &&\n       opts.method === \"POST\"\n     ) {\n       const body = JSON.parse(opts.body as string)\n       if (body.store !== true && Array.isArray(body.input)) {\n         for (const item of body.input) {\n           if (\"id\" in item) delete item.id\n         }\n         opts.body = JSON.stringify(body)\n       }\n     }\n\n     const res = await (typeof customFetch === \"function\" ? customFetch : fetch)(input, {\n       ...opts,\n       timeout: false,\n     })\n-    if (!chunkAbortCtl || typeof chunkTimeout !== \"number\") return res\n-    return wrapSSE(res, chunkTimeout, chunkAbortCtl)\n+    const isSSE = res.headers.get(\"content-type\")?.includes(\"text/event-stream\")\n+    if (isSSE) {\n+      if (!chunkAbortCtl || typeof chunkTimeout !== \"number\") return res\n+      return wrapSSE(res, chunkTimeout, chunkAbortCtl)\n+    }\n+    if (!bodyIdleAbortCtl || typeof bodyIdleTimeout !== \"number\") return res\n+    return wrapBodyIdle(res, bodyIdleTimeout, bodyIdleAbortCtl, bodyAbsoluteTimeout)\n   }\n```\n\n**Compile + behavior check (v1.18.13):** `abortSignals` is `AbortSignal[]` (the original `signals` array minus the controller extraction); `chunkAbortCtl` and `bodyIdleAbortCtl` are both declared before use; with both knobs set the composed signal is `AbortSignal.any([…chunk.signal, …body.signal, …timeout])`; with only one knob set the correct controller is bound (the `find` aliasing hazard is gone); with neither set, behavior is byte-identical to stock (both undefined → `abortSignals` = `[opts.signal?, timeout?]`).\n\n**v2 error-class note (kept from #180, re-verified):** `aiskd.ts` raises a plain `Error`; the v2 plugin AISDK path does not route through `MessageV2.fromError` (v2 `SessionRunner` uses `LLMError` from `@opencode-ai/llm`), so the plain-`Error` distinction does not affect the v1 retry analysis. The v2 patch's job is purely termination. Documented v2-path limitation: no `headerTimeout` on the v2 hook path — re-checked on every rebase (§6.5).\n\n### 2.3 Patch C — `packages/opencode/src/session/retry.ts` — budget + observability (B3, F4, V5, F-new-1)\n\n**Hunk C1 — constants + helpers (after `RETRY_MAX_DELAY` at L17):**\n\n```diff\n export const RETRY_INITIAL_DELAY = 2000\n export const RETRY_BACKOFF_FACTOR = 2\n export const RETRY_MAX_DELAY_NO_HEADERS = 30_000 // 30 seconds\n export const RETRY_MAX_DELAY = 2_147_483_647 // max 32-bit signed integer for setTimeout\n+export const RETRY_MAX_RETRIES = 2 // bounded timeout/stream class: initial + 2 retries = exactly 3 POSTs\n+\n+// Error codes whose retries are bounded by RETRY_MAX_RETRIES. Everything else\n+// (429 / usage-limit / 5xx / plain APIErrors) keeps the existing unbounded\n+// retry-after semantics. ZlibError is included: a deterministic decompression\n+// failure must not retry forever (it is the failure most likely to be\n+// introduced by re-wrapping a compressed body).\n+const RETRY_BOUNDED_CODES = new Set([\n+  \"ProviderResponseStreamError\",\n+  \"ProviderHeaderTimeoutError\",\n+  \"ECONNRESET\",\n+  \"ZlibError\",\n+])\n+\n+function retryCode(error: Err) {\n+  return SessionV1.APIError.isInstance(error)\n+    ? error.data.metadata?.code ?? error.data.message\n+    : String(error)\n+}\n+\n+function isBoundedRetryCode(error: Err) {\n+  return (\n+    SessionV1.APIError.isInstance(error) &&\n+    typeof error.data.metadata?.code === \"string\" &&\n+    RETRY_BOUNDED_CODES.has(error.data.metadata.code)\n+  )\n+}\n```\n\n**Hunk C2 — `policy()` step (L176–199) — budget stop + per-attempt WARN + Effect-aware terminal WARN (V5 CLOSED):**\n\n```diff\n export function policy(opts: {\n   provider: string\n   parse: (error: unknown) => Err\n   set: (input: { attempt: number; message: string; action?: Retryable[\"action\"]; next: number }) => Effect.Effect<void>\n }) {\n   return Schedule.fromStepWithMetadata(\n     Effect.succeed((meta: Schedule.InputMetadata<unknown>) => {\n       const error = opts.parse(meta.input)\n       const retry = retryable(error, opts.provider)\n       if (!retry) return Cause.done(meta.attempt)\n+      if (meta.attempt > RETRY_MAX_RETRIES && isBoundedRetryCode(error)) {\n+        // Budget exhausted for the timeout/stream class. meta.attempt is a\n+        // 1-based RETRY count; at this stop point (attempt > 2) the total\n+        // POST count is initial + 2 retries = 3 = meta.attempt — NOT\n+        // meta.attempt + 1. The WARN is an Effect, so it runs on the\n+        // Cause.done path (Effect.andThen chains it before failing with Done).\n+        return Effect.logWarning(\"retry budget exhausted\", {\n+          provider: opts.provider,\n+          attempt: meta.attempt,\n+          totalPOSTs: meta.attempt,\n+          code: retryCode(error),\n+        }).pipe(Effect.andThen(() => Cause.done(meta.attempt)))\n+      }\n       return Effect.gen(function* () {\n         const wait = delay(meta.attempt, SessionV1.APIError.isInstance(error) ? error : undefined)\n         const now = yield* Clock.currentTimeMillis\n+        yield* Effect.logWarning(\"retry\", {\n+          provider: opts.provider,\n+          attempt: meta.attempt,\n+          code: retryCode(error),\n+          nextDelay: wait,\n+        })\n         yield* opts.set({\n           attempt: meta.attempt,\n           message: retry.message,\n           action: retry.action,\n           next: now + wait,\n         })\n         return [meta.attempt, Duration.millis(wait)] as [number, Duration.Duration]\n       })\n     }),\n   )\n }\n```\n\n**V5 placement/arithmetic (both r1 V5.1/V5.2 and r3 B3-1 closed):**\n- **Arithmetic**: `totalPOSTs: meta.attempt`. At the stop point `meta.attempt = 3` (stop at `> 2`), and POSTs performed = initial + 2 retries = 3. The #180 `meta.attempt + 1` would have printed 4 — the exact off-by-one the design is meant to eliminate. Invariant: server-side POST counter ≤ 3 = `meta.attempt` at the terminal WARN (test 14 asserts both).\n- **Placement**: `Cause.done(meta.attempt)` at retry.ts:185 is a synchronous return inside `Effect.succeed((meta) => …)`; `yield* Effect.logWarning` cannot be placed on that path as written. The fix wraps the log in an Effect and chains it with `Effect.andThen(() => Cause.done(meta.attempt))` — `Cause.done` returns `Effect<never, Done<number>>` (verified: `Cause.d.ts:1472`), `Pull<…>` accepts it in the error channel (verified: `Pull.d.ts:36`), so the step's return type is preserved and the schedule semantics are unchanged (a `Done` in the error channel stops the schedule, exactly like the current plain return).\n- **Scope**: the terminal WARN fires only for the bounded class (budget exhausted). Non-retryable errors (`if (!retry)`) keep the silent stock stop — a 401 is not a \"budget exhausted\" condition.\n- **Per-attempt WARN (F4)**: inside the existing `Effect.gen`, where `wait`/`now` are in scope; `Effect.logWarning(\"retry\", { provider, attempt, code, nextDelay })` follows the exact variadic-object pattern already used at llm.ts:283 (`Effect.logError(\"stream error\", {…})`), so it compiles and emits structured `level=WARN` lines (grep-asserted by test 13).\n- **retry-after preservation (unchanged)**: the unbounded class (429/usage-limit/5xx/plain APIErrors) never hits the budget branch — `isBoundedRetryCode` is false, so the existing `delay()` retry-after honoring is untouched.\n\n### 2.4 Patch D — `packages/opencode/src/session/llm.ts` — turn-level guard (F5-1 CLOSED, F-new-5 CLOSED)\n\n**Hunk D1 — imports (L7–8):**\n\n```diff\n-import { Context, Effect, Layer } from \"effect\"\n+import { Context, Duration, Effect, Layer } from \"effect\"\n import * as Stream from \"effect/Stream\"\n+import { ProviderError } from \"@/provider/error\"\n```\n\n**Hunk D2 — stream composition (L371–377). The guard is now MANDATORY (F-new-5), and uses `Stream.timeoutOrElse` (F5-1):**\n\n```diff\n             const state = LLMAISDK.adapterState()\n+            const llmIdleTimeout = cfg.experimental?.llmIdleTimeout ?? 300_000\n             return Stream.fromAsyncIterable(result.result.fullStream, (e) =>\n               e instanceof Error ? e : new Error(String(e)),\n             ).pipe(\n+              // MANDATORY turn-level idle-progress guard (the only mechanism\n+              // that bounds the production 10.9 h signature: parsed-event\n+              // stalls above the raw-body layer). Stream.timeoutOrElse is\n+              // verified in effect 4.0.0-beta.83 with per-pull idle semantics\n+              // (\"The timeout is checked for each pull\") — it resets on every\n+              // parsed event, exactly the required behavior. Stream.timeoutFail\n+              // does NOT exist in this version.\n+              Stream.timeoutOrElse({\n+                duration: Duration.millis(llmIdleTimeout),\n+                orElse: () =>\n+                  Stream.fail(\n+                    new ProviderError.ResponseStreamError(\n+                      `Turn stalled: no parsed stream event within ${llmIdleTimeout}ms`,\n+                    ),\n+                  ),\n+              }),\n               Stream.mapEffect((event) => LLMAISDK.toLLMEvents(state, event)),\n               Stream.flatMap((events) => Stream.fromIterable(events)),\n             )\n```\n\nThe `ResponseStreamError` (code `ProviderResponseStreamError`) thrown here flows into the same bounded retry budget (Patch C) — the raw-body and parsed-stream deadlines are one coherent idle-progress policy across layers.\n\n**Hunk D3 — instrumentation (kept from #180 §5.2.1, mandatory):** at stream start in the same composition, log response metadata (content-type, transport, provider/model/session) and emit a per-parsed-event DEBUG progress line (elapsed-since-last-parsed-event). The real-provider capture (test 15) then records the actual stall layer; the *next* hang is self-identifying.\n\n### 2.5 Patch E — config schemas (F-new-3 CLOSED)\n\n**Hunk E1 — `packages/core/src/v1/config/provider.ts` (after the `chunkTimeout` entry, before the `Schema.Record` rest):**\n\n```diff\n         chunkTimeout: Schema.optional(PositiveInt).annotate({\n           description:\n             \"Timeout in milliseconds between streamed SSE chunks for this provider. If no chunk arrives within this window, the request is aborted.\",\n         }),\n+        bodyIdleTimeout: Schema.optional(PositiveInt).annotate({\n+          description:\n+            \"Timeout in milliseconds between chunks of a non-SSE response body for this provider. If no chunk arrives within this window, the request is aborted. Idle-progress deadline, distinct from chunkTimeout: slow-but-progressing bodies are never aborted.\",\n+        }),\n+        bodyAbsoluteTimeout: Schema.optional(PositiveInt).annotate({\n+          description:\n+            \"Optional total wall-clock cap in milliseconds for a non-SSE response body. Off by default; when set, a body that runs longer than this is aborted regardless of progress.\",\n+        }),\n```\n\n**Hunk E2 — `packages/core/src/v1/config/config.ts` (inside the `experimental` Struct, after `mcp_timeout`):**\n\n```diff\n       mcp_timeout: Schema.optional(PositiveInt).annotate({\n         description: \"Timeout in milliseconds for model context protocol (MCP) requests\",\n       }),\n+      llmIdleTimeout: Schema.optional(PositiveInt).annotate({\n+        description:\n+          \"Timeout in milliseconds between parsed stream events from the language model. If no parsed event arrives within this window, the request is aborted (turn-level idle-progress guard; default 300000).\",\n+      }),\n```\n\n**Rationale (F-new-3):** the schema's `Schema.Record(Schema.String, Schema.Any)` rest already accepted `bodyIdleTimeout` — and silently accepted `bodyIdletimeout` too. For a knob whose entire purpose is hang protection, silent typo tolerance re-creates \"protection silently absent\". Declaring the keys gives validation errors + editor completion. Implementation step: regenerate `packages/sdk/openapi.json` from the schema via the repo's generator after editing (the schema is the source of truth; openapi.json is generated).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Non-SSE deadline and numeric chain (B2, V4 CLOSED)\n\n### 3.1 Mechanism (unchanged from #180 — Option A')\n\n`bodyIdleTimeout` (idle-progress, resets per chunk; slow-but-progressing bodies never aborted) for the non-SSE branch, distinct from `chunkTimeout` (SSE). Optional `bodyAbsoluteTimeout` belt-and-braces total cap, default OFF. Patch A/B implement it; the Option-B false-abort class analysis from #180 §3.4 is retained.\n\n### 3.2 Numeric chain — re-derived against the PROJECT's 15–20 m operator-timeout ladder (V4 CLOSED)\n\nThe #180 chain compared a *chain total* (30 min) against a *per-request* bound (60 min request `timeout`) and then against an assumed 1 h operator timeout — the wrong ladder. SESSION-START §4a fixes task-matched operator-timeout ceilings: trivial ≤10 m, doc/simple/review **15–20 m**, port/multi-file 30 m, complex multi-phase 45 m+.\n\n**Production values:**\n\n| Knob | Value | Relation |\n|---|---|---|\n| `bodyIdleTimeout` | **300 000 ms (5 min)** — parity with production `chunkTimeout` | per-request idle < request `timeout` (5 min < 60 min) ✔ |\n| `bodyAbsoluteTimeout` | 3 300 000 ms (55 min), **opt-in, default OFF** | < request `timeout` (55 min < 60 min) ✔ |\n| `RETRY_MAX_RETRIES` | 2 (⇒ exactly 3 POSTs for the bounded class) | — |\n| Worst case to terminal ERROR | `300 000 × 3` = **15 min** (+ ~6 s backoff) | **≤ 15 m floor** of the 15–20 m doc/review tier; **< 20 m** ceiling; **< 30 m / 45 m+** longer tiers |\n\n**Invariant (the rule r1 asked for):**\n`bodyIdleTimeout × (RETRY_MAX_RETRIES + 1) ≤ smallest operator timeout in use (15 m floor of the 15–20 m tier)` — 15 min ≤ 15 min. Equality at the floor is by design: it is exactly the SSE path's worst case (production `chunkTimeout=300000` ⇒ 15-min SSE detection), so non-SSE detection latency is **parity, not 2× slower** (the asymmetry r1 flagged). Strict `<` holds against the 20 m ceiling and every longer tier.\n\n**Recorded exception — trivial ≤10 m tier:** for tasks launched at ≤10 m, the operator kill fires before the terminal ERROR surfaces (15 min > 10 min). Their protection is the outer net (operator timeout + #146 watcher restart) **plus** the per-attempt WARN lines emitted at ~5-min cadence — the failure is no longer silent (the pre-fix signature was an unbounded silent hang). This is the documented, accepted exception for the shortest tier; every task ≥ 15 m sees the ERROR before any outer kill.\n\n**Per-attempt ceiling:** each POST is bounded by the first of {`bodyIdleTimeout` fire (5 min idle), `bodyAbsoluteTimeout` if set (55 min), request `timeout` (60 min)} — in every realistic hang the idle timer fires first.\n\n**Alternative strict-form one-knob** (recorded, not primary): if strict `<` at the 15 m floor is ever demanded, `bodyIdleTimeout = 240 000` (4 min ⇒ 12 min < 15 min strictly) is the single change; cost is non-SSE detection 20% faster than SSE (asymmetry in the safe direction).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Verification matrix — self-consistent harness (R2, V2, F5-2 CLOSED)\n\n### 4.1 Harness cfg (V2 CLOSED)\n\nThe #180 harness kept `timeout: 15000` while adding `bodyIdleTimeout: 30000` — `bodyIdleTimeout` > `timeout`, so the request-level `AbortSignal.timeout` always fired first and the new deadline was **unobservable**; test 6's 20–25 s slow body would false-abort at 15 s and test 9 was unrunnable. The corrected base cfg enforces the invariant **`headerTimeout < chunkTimeout < bodyIdleTimeout < timeout`**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://opencode.ai/config.json\",\n  \"provider\": {\n    \"hangtest\": {\n      \"npm\": \"@ai-sdk/openai-compatible\",\n      \"options\": {\n        \"baseURL\": \"http://127.0.0.1:8777/v1\",\n        \"apiKey\": \"test\",\n        \"headerTimeout\": 2000,\n        \"chunkTimeout\": 3000,\n        \"bodyIdleTimeout\": 6000,\n        \"timeout\": 60000\n      },\n      \"models\": {\n        \"hang-model\": {\n          \"name\": \"hang-model\",\n          \"limit\": { \"context\": 16000, \"output\": 4096 },\n          \"cost\": { \"input\": 1, \"output\": 1 }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- `2000 < 3000 < 6000 < 60000` ✔ — the request timeout (60 s) now **exceeds** the body-idle deadline, so `wrapBodyIdle` is the mechanism that fires on dead bodies.\n- The brief's example pair (`bodyIdleTimeout=30000`, `timeout=60000`) also satisfies `timeout > bodyIdleTimeout`; r1's recommended `6000` is adopted because it keeps test-6's 25 s total comfortably under 60 s and keeps per-test detection latency tight (1 s margin between the 5 s gaps and the 6 s idle threshold).\n- **Per-test cfg overrides** (needed by rows 8/9/9b): the runner generates a temp `OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR` per test from the base cfg + row-specific option overrides via a small `gen-cfg.mjs` (base JSON + `Object.assign` on `provider.hangtest.options` + optional `experimental`). Each row below states its overrides explicitly — no row relies on the base values implicitly.\n- **server.js additions** (from #180, kept): `SLOW_CHUNK_MS` env (inter-chunk delays, test 6), `PER_REQUEST` mode (req 1 hangs, req 2 healthy, test 7), `GZIP` env (gzip non-SSE body, test 10), `STALLED` mode (fixed-interval chunks, test 9), `PARSE_STALL` mode (SSE with comment keepalives, test 9b).\n\n### 4.2 Matrix — every row re-derived against the corrected cfg\n\nWorst-case budget in the harness: `bodyIdleTimeout (6 s) × 3 POSTs` ≈ 18–24 s + backoff < `timeout` 60 s ✔ (each POST is bounded by the first of {6 s idle, 60 s request timeout}).\n\n| # | Scenario | Parameters (incl. overrides) | Expected | Proves |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | application/json + hang | mode 1, ct=application/json, base cfg | abort at ~6 s idle (`bodyIdleTimeout` — the NEW mechanism, not the 15 s request timeout); ≤3 POSTs; grep-asserted ERROR; non-zero exit (not EXIT 124) | non-SSE hang killed; budget; error surfacing |\n| 2 | text/event-stream + hang | mode 1, ct=text/event-stream | abort at ~3 s (`chunkTimeout`, unchanged); ≤3 POSTs; ERROR | SSE path unchanged; budget |\n| 3 | no response at all | mode 0 | `headerTimeout` fires at ~2 s; 4 `ProviderHeaderTimeoutError` entries | headerTimeout untouched |\n| 4 | healthy application/json | complete body | EXIT 0, no retries, no abort | no regression |\n| 5 | healthy text/event-stream | mode 2 | \"Hello world\", EXIT 0, no retries | no regression |\n| 6 | **slow-but-legit non-SSE** | `SLOW_CHUNK_MS=5000`, 5 chunks ⇒ 5×5 s gaps, 25 s total; gaps (5 s) **> `chunkTimeout` (3 s)** and **< `bodyIdleTimeout` (6 s)**; total 25 s **< `timeout` (60 s)** | completes, EXIT 0, no abort | hy3 F2 preserved; discriminates A' from A (Option A would false-abort at a 3 s gap) |\n| 6b | slow-but-legit non-SSE, never completes | same server minus final chunk | abort at ≤6 s idle (`bodyIdleTimeout`) | non-SSE deadline kills dead bodies |\n| 7 | per-request abort | `PER_REQUEST`: req 1 hangs, req 2 healthy | healthy completes unaffected; aborted request's signal/reason isolated | hy3 F4 (regression guard; source-confirmed `new AbortController()` per-call at provider.ts:1746) |\n| 8 | bodyIdleTimeout sensitivity | override `bodyIdleTimeout: 2000` vs `4000` | retry cadence tracks the knob (~2 s vs ~4 s abort) | mechanism is the config knob |\n| 9 | **stalled-but-not-dead** | `STALLED` chunks every 15 s; override `bodyIdleTimeout: 10000`; total run ≤ 30 s < 60 s | aborts at 10 s idle — the A' idle fires, NOT a total cap (Option B would wait for a total that A' does not have); discriminates A' from B | the test r1 said \"would have surfaced B2\" — now runnable |\n| 9b | **parsed-stream stall** (F5-2 pinned) | `PARSE_STALL`: SSE headers + **SSE comment keepalives `: ping\\n\\n` every 500 ms** (raw cadence continues ⇒ raw `wrapSSE`/`chunkTimeout` never fires) while **no `data:` event ever arrives** (parsed events stop); override `experimental.llmIdleTimeout: 5000` | turn-level guard fires `ResponseStreamError(\"Turn stalled…\")` at ~5 s; ≤3 POSTs; ERROR | the production layer (#39968) — cannot pass via the raw layer (the false-positive route r3 flagged) |\n| 10 | gzip non-SSE body | `GZIP` healthy + `GZIP` hang | healthy completes with **no double-decode/length error** (headers stripped per F-new-2); hang aborts at ≤6 s idle | compressed bodies safe under the wrapper |\n| 11 | non-chat request | non-chat endpoint, non-SSE content-type | passes through; with `bodyIdleTimeout` unconfigured → unwrapped (opt-in); configured → completes | opt-in wrapping doesn't break non-chat traffic |\n| 12 | fork unit tests | `retry.test.ts` + `body-idle-timeout.test.ts` | see §4.3 | divergence protected across rebases |\n| 13 | grep-assert ERROR | after each hang test | ≥1 `level=ERROR` line + per-attempt `level=WARN message=\"retry\"` + terminal `level=WARN message=\"retry budget exhausted\"` | error visibility is assertable, not eyeballed |\n| 14 | POST counts, not attempt indices | server-side counter | ≤3 POSTs for hang scenarios; terminal WARN `totalPOSTs` = server count (both = 3) | invariant in the observable quantity (V5) |\n| 15 | real-provider capture | one instrumented `opencode run` vs real `opencode-go` | records content-type/transport/last-progress; no regression on a normal call | identifies the production stall layer |\n| 16 | **v2 copy acceptance (F-new-9b)** | static grep on the fork source | `wrapBodyIdle` present in **both** `provider.ts` and `aisdk.ts`; content-type guard count = **0** in both; `signals.find` absent from `aisdk.ts prepareOptions` | Patch B (the unreachable-in-runtime v2 copy) verified by the §6.5 static criteria promoted to an explicit acceptance row |\n\n### 4.3 Fork unit tests (F-new-9a CLOSED — concrete files)\n\n**`packages/opencode/test/session/retry.test.ts`** (existing file, extended):\n1. Bounded-class cap: `ResponseStreamError`-coded error retried at attempts 1 and 2, `Cause.done` at attempt 3 — assert the step returns done after `meta.attempt > 2` and the terminal WARN emitted with `totalPOSTs = 3`.\n2. Unbounded-class preserved: 429 `retry-after` error still honors the header (the upstream \"exceeding 10 minutes\" test must still pass unchanged).\n3. Off-by-one regression: delay sequence `[2000, 4000]` then stop for the bounded class (3 POSTs total).\n4. Per-attempt logging: the step emits a WARN per attempt with attempt/code/nextDelay (captured Effect logger).\n5. `ZlibError` bounded: a `ZlibError`-coded error stops at attempt 3 (F-new-1).\n\n**`packages/opencode/test/provider/body-idle-timeout.test.ts`** (NEW — template: `header-timeout.test.ts`, which already has `it.live(\"chunkTimeout raises a response stream error when SSE body stalls\")` + a `delayedBodyServer` fixture; reuse that pattern with a non-SSE content-type):\n1. Idle fires on gap > ms (non-SSE body stalls → `ResponseStreamError(\"Body read timed out\")`).\n2. Slow progress (gaps < ms) does not fire.\n3. `done`/`cancel` clear both timers (assert no timer leak: idle + absolute armed state).\n4. Absolute cap fires only when configured, and **errors the stream deterministically** (V3 regression guard — the #180 defect).\n5. Dispatcher routes SSE → `wrapSSE`, non-SSE → `wrapBodyIdle`, unconfigured → unwrapped; absent content-type → non-SSE branch.\n6. Headers: synthesized Response has `content-length`/`content-encoding` stripped (F-new-2).\n\n### 4.4 Retained r2 additional checks\n\nWrapper survival (flip `REAL` to fork, simulate npm upgrade, assert fork still resolves + `autoupdate:false` effective); consumer-cancellation mid-body (timers cleared); exit-code verification on session error (`opencode run` non-zero — remains an assumption to be confirmed, as flagged in #180).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Minor findings — resolution table (F-new-1..9, B1-1, B3-1, F5-3)\n\n| Finding | Source | Resolution | Where |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F-new-1 `ZlibError` in unbounded class ⇒ infinite retry | message-v2.ts:638–651 | Added `\"ZlibError\"` to `RETRY_BOUNDED_CODES` | Patch C |\n| F-new-2 header passthrough undecided | #182 | Decision: **strip `content-length` + `content-encoding`** on the synthesized Response (fetch() has already decoded the body; a re-chunked stream does not match the stale headers; keeping them risks double-decode → ZlibError). Empirical validation stays in test 10. | Patch A/B |\n| F-new-3 no config schema | #182 | Added schema entries: `bodyIdleTimeout`, `bodyAbsoluteTimeout` (provider), `experimental.llmIdleTimeout` (config). Typo-tolerant rest still accepts arbitrary keys — the declared entries are what give validation/editor support. Regenerate `packages/sdk/openapi.json`. | Patch E |\n| F-new-4 F11 citation wrong | #182 | Corrected: bun gate is `packages/script/src/index.ts:5–18`, `semver.satisfies(process.versions.bun, \"^1.3.14\")` (caret range from root `packageManager`), imported via `@opencode-ai/script`. `packages/opencode/script/script.ts` does not exist. | §6.2 |\n| F-new-5 F5 guard \"(recommended)\" | #182 | Guard is **MANDATORY** — it is the only mechanism that bounds the production signature. | Patch D |\n| F-new-6 `OPENCODE_CHANNEL=fork-pp3g` ⇒ `IS_PREVIEW` | #182 | Verified inert: `upgrade.ts:10` `if (config.autoupdate === false \\|\\| Flag.OPENCODE_DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE) return` short-circuits before `getReleaseType`; `getReleaseType` compares semver major/minor only (`installation/index.ts:24–36`) so `1.18.13-pp3g-fork` is classified against 1.18.x normally; `IS_PREVIEW` only affects the VERSION fallback when `OPENCODE_VERSION` is unset — we always set it. Documented as accepted; no change. | §6.4 |\n| F-new-7 drift-check spawn cost | #182 | Acknowledged + accepted: the wrapper already spawns `\"$REAL\" models` every launch; §6.4 adds one `\"$REAL\" --version` spawn (~sub-second local process) per launch. Folded into the SAME guarded launch block so the marker check runs before any agent work; cost is bounded and immaterial vs agent runtime. Alternative (embedded-string `grep` on the binary) documented if spawn cost is ever a concern. | §6.4 |\n| F-new-8 TUI message mapping | #182 | Documented: `tui/…/notifications.ts:23` exact-matches `\"SSE read timed out\"`; `\"Body read timed out\"` / `\"Turn stalled…\"` fall through to generic \"Session error\". Off our `opencode run` path; informational. Optional future mapping noted (`data.message === \"Body read timed out\" \\|\\| data.message.startsWith(\"Turn stalled\")`). | §6.5 |\n| F-new-9 matrix gaps | #182 | (a) `wrapBodyIdle` unit tests named: **`packages/opencode/test/provider/body-idle-timeout.test.ts`** on the `header-timeout.test.ts` template; (b) v2 copy has **no runtime row** (unreachable on our path) ⇒ matrix row **16** promotes the §6.5 static grep-counts to explicit acceptance. | §4.2/4.3 |\n| B1-1 (= V1) | #184 | Hunk 4 finalized: `bodyIdleAbortCtl` declared; both controllers named; no `signals.find`. | Patch B |\n| B3-1 (= V5.1) | #184 | `totalPOSTs: meta.attempt` (3, not 4). | Patch C |\n| F5-3 §5.1 causal premise | #184 | Corrected attribution: the 15 s harness kill was the **shell-level GNU `timeout \"$OUTER\" …`** around `opencode run` (verified `run-test.sh`; EXIT 124 = GNU timeout's code), not `AbortSignal.timeout` — retained `run-json.out` shows no \"operation timed out\" message. The turn-level guard is justified as defense-in-depth: it fires on parsed-event stall **regardless of the raw-body layer state**, so it covers both interpretations. | §2.4 |\n| `aiskd.ts` / `aisdk.ts` typo | #182 B1-2, #184 B1-2 | Corrected **everywhere** (file is `packages/core/src/aisdk.ts`); the §6.5 rebase checklist now names the real path. | all sections |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Build / replace / rollback (unchanged from #180 where CLOSED — corrections only)\n\n### 6.1 Step 0 — interim mitigation status\n\n`autoupdate: false` set + #179 byte patch live on both copies (re-verified §0). Implementation step 0: re-verify the stopgap before/during the fork build (a manual npm upgrade would wipe it); keep it until the fork binary is live.\n\n### 6.2 Build prereqs (F11 — corrected per F-new-4)\n\n```bash\n# 1. bun, PINNED to the repo's packageManager (root package.json: \"bun@1.3.14\").\n#    The version gate lives in packages/script/src/index.ts:5-18 (^1.3.14 caret\n#    range, enforced via semver.satisfies on the root packageManager value) and\n#    is imported as @opencode-ai/script. NOT packages/opencode/script/script.ts.\ncurl -fsSL https://bun.sh/install | bash -s -- bun-v1.3.14    # verify exact pin flag at implementation\n\n# 2. clone fork (canonical upstream, pinned tag) and apply the patch\ngit clone https://github.com/<org>/opencode-fork.git\ncd opencode-fork && git checkout v1.18.13 && git apply opencode-154-durable.patch   # Patches A-E\n\n# 3. install at the WORKSPACE ROOT (root package.json declares workspaces; root\n#    postinstall runs `bun run --cwd packages/core fix-node-pty`)\nbun install                                    # at repo root, NOT inside packages/opencode\n\n# 4. build single-target binary\ncd packages/opencode\nOPENCODE_VERSION=1.18.13-pp3g-fork OPENCODE_CHANNEL=fork-pp3g bun run build --single\n\n# 5. smoke test\n./dist/opencode-linux-x64/bin/opencode --version   # expect 1.18.13-pp3g-fork\n```\n\n- `--skip-embed-web-ui` decision (kept): build WITHOUT the flag first; accept it only if the embedded web app build fails/slows (degrades only the embedded web dashboard; TUI + `opencode run` unaffected — web UI is a separate embedded bundle). Record the decision in `.crosslink/knowledge/opencode-fork.md`.\n- `bun install` must run at the root (postinstall + workspace resolution).\n\n### 6.3 Replace / rollback (unchanged — stage + same-fs `mv`, the #145-proven atomic pattern)\n\nKept verbatim from #180 §6.2/§6.3: backup stock 1.18.13 → rotate previous fork → stage `.opencode.exe.new` → atomic `mv` → wrapper `REAL` → fork binary. Rollback symmetric; criterion: any provider regression → restore stock + report; #146 watcher remains the safety net.\n\n### 6.4 Fork-identity marker + drift detection (F12; F-new-6/F-new-7 dispositions)\n\n- **Marker**: build with `OPENCODE_VERSION=1.18.13-pp3g-fork OPENCODE_CHANNEL=fork-pp3g` ⇒ `--version` shows the fork marker (verified chain: script env → build.ts defines → `InstallationVersion`). Runtime string marker `\"Body read timed out\"` embedded in both patched copies.\n- **Drift detection (F-new-7)**: extend `~/.local/bin/opencode` — before `exec \"$REAL\" \"$@\"`, run `\"$REAL\" --version` and assert the fork marker; on mismatch, loud stderr + `exit 1`. Cost: one extra sub-second spawn per launch, accepted (see §5). Same assertion added to the #146 watcher's periodic check.\n- **F-new-6**: no change required — `autoupdate:false` short-circuits `upgrade.ts:10` before any `getReleaseType`/prerelease comparison; `IS_PREVIEW` is inert because `OPENCODE_VERSION` is always set.\n\n### 6.5 Rebase discipline (corrected paths — `aisdk.ts`, not `aiskd.ts`)\n\n`.crosslink/knowledge/opencode-fork.md` holds: upstream identity, pinned tag, both patches, build/replace/rollback, marker + drift-check, and the invariant \"any upgrade = rebuild the fork at the new tag and re-apply both patches\". Rebase checklist (the static criteria are ALSO matrix row 16):\n1. `provider.ts` + **`aisdk.ts`** content-type guard count = 0 each.\n2. `wrapBodyIdle` marker present in **both** `provider.ts` and **`aisdk.ts`**; `signals.find` absent from `aisdk.ts prepareOptions`.\n3. fork `--version` marker present.\n4. §4 unit tests green.\n5. re-verify the v2 reachability assumption (§2.2).\n\n---\n\n## 7. Change-log vs #180\n\n| #180 | Round 3 (#186) | Driver |\n|---|---|---|\n| §2.3 Hunk 4 (aiskd.ts): `bodyIdleAbortCtl` undeclared + `signals.find` aliasing, \"must be finalised against the exact source\" | **Final compilable Patch B**: both controllers explicitly named, `signals.find` removed, verified against v1.18.13 source | **V1** / B1-1 |\n| §7.1 harness `timeout: 15000` + `bodyIdleTimeout: 30000` (deadline can never fire; test 6 guaranteed fail; test 9 unrunnable) | **Self-consistent cfg** `2000 < 3000 < 6000 < 60000` + per-test overrides (gen-cfg) + every row re-derived (test 6: 5 s gaps > 3 s chunkTimeout, 25 s < 60 s; test 9: 15 s gaps, `bodyIdleTimeout=10000`, ≤ 30 s run) | **V2** / R2 |\n| `wrapBodyIdle` absolute-cap callback: no stream controller (consumer read never settles) + `absoluteId` not cleared on idle path (timer leak) | **Shared `fail()`**: stream controller captured in `start()`, `streamCtl?.error(err)` terminates deterministically even pre-first-pull; both timers cleared on every path | **V3** / F7 |\n| §3.3 numeric chain vs 1 h request `timeout` and 1 h operator timeout | **Re-derived vs SESSION-START §4a ladder**: `bodyIdleTimeout=300000` (parity with `chunkTimeout`) ⇒ 15-min worst case ≤ 15 m floor, < 20 m ceiling and all longer tiers; trivial ≤10 m exception recorded (outer net + per-attempt WARNs) | **V4** / B2 |\n| §4.2.1 terminal WARN `total POSTs: meta.attempt + 1` (=4) on a synchronous non-Effect path | **Effect-aware terminal WARN** via `Effect.andThen(() => Cause.done(meta.attempt))`; `totalPOSTs: meta.attempt` (=3) | **V5** / B3-1 |\n| §5.2 `Stream.timeoutFail({…})` — does not compile (API absent in effect 4.0.0-beta.83) | **`Stream.timeoutOrElse({ duration, orElse: () => Stream.fail(new ProviderError.ResponseStreamError(\"Turn stalled…\")) })`** — verified present with per-pull idle semantics | **F5-1** |\n| §7.1 test 9b underspecified (can pass via raw `chunkTimeout`) | **Pinned**: `PARSE_STALL` mode = SSE headers + `: ping` comment keepalives every 500 ms (raw cadence continues, parsed events stop) + `experimental.llmIdleTimeout: 5000` | **F5-2** |\n| §4 unbounded class admits `ZlibError` (infinite retry) | `ZlibError` added to `RETRY_BOUNDED_CODES` | F-new-1 |\n| §2 header passthrough undecided | Strip `content-length` + `content-encoding` on synthesized Response | F-new-2 |\n| (absent) | Patch E: `bodyIdleTimeout`/`bodyAbsoluteTimeout`/`experimental.llmIdleTimeout` schema entries + openapi regeneration note | F-new-3 |\n| §6.1 \"packages/opencode/script/script.ts enforces ^1.3.14\" | Corrected: `packages/script/src/index.ts:5–18` (caret range) | F-new-4 |\n| §5.2 turn-level guard \"(recommended)\" | **Mandatory** | F-new-5 |\n| (absent) | `OPENCODE_CHANNEL`/`IS_PREVIEW` interaction analyzed; inert under `autoupdate:false` (`upgrade.ts:10`); no change | F-new-6 |\n| §6.4 drift-check adds a spawn | Cost acknowledged + accepted (one sub-second `--version` spawn; alternative binary-grep noted) | F-new-7 |\n| (absent) | TUI `notifications.ts:23` exact-match mapping documented; new messages → generic \"Session error\" (off our path) | F-new-8 |\n| §7.3 item 5 names no unit-test file; no v2 runtime row | **`body-idle-timeout.test.ts`** (header-timeout template) + matrix row **16** static acceptance for the v2 copy | F-new-9 |\n| §5.1 \"15 s = AbortSignal.timeout firing\" | Corrected: shell-level GNU `timeout \"$OUTER\"` (`run-test.sh`; EXIT 124); guard justified as any-layer defense-in-depth | F5-3 |\n| \"aiskd.ts\" everywhere | **`aisdk.ts`** everywhere (incl. §6.5 rebase checklist) | B1-2 |\n| (kept, CLOSED in round 2) | Both-copy patch decision + reachability evidence; Option A' idle shape; class-scoped budget semantics; retry-after preservation; pull() shape + backpressure; opt-in semantics; atomic install; root bun install + pin; fork marker + drift; step-0 stopgap; PER_REQUEST mode | #182/#184 |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Open items / handoff\n\n- **Implementer**: apply Patches A–E to the fork @ v1.18.13, regenerate `packages/sdk/openapi.json` from the edited schemas, build per §6.2, run the §4 matrix + unit tests, install per §6.3, write `.crosslink/knowledge/opencode-fork.md`; keep step-0 stopgap verified; run `bun typecheck` after each patch hunk (Patch B was the compile risk; the design's hunk is final, but typecheck is the gate).\n- **Reviewer**: re-check only the corrected items per both verdicts' guidance: Patch B (V1/B1-1), terminal WARN arithmetic + placement (V5/B3-1), `wrapBodyIdle` absolute-cap lifecycle (V3), numeric chain (V4), harness cfg + rows 6/9/9b (V2/F5-2), F5 guard API (F5-1), and the minor-finding dispositions (§5).\n- **Upstream tracking**: PR #39516 (chunkTimeout for every streamed body), PR #35743 (eventstream matching), issue #39968 (parsed-stream stalls) remain the long-term fixes; the fork is the pinned divergence until they land.\n- **Immediate operational note**: box remains protected by the ephemeral #179 byte patch + `autoupdate:false`; the durable fork install remains high-priority.","created_at":"2026-08-05T23:46:24.554476087Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:zxgneOQcVg1KKV9+QJPuhXyXWdXIm2Iblibtm/YNSbY","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYZ+rHmf04iTJEStjmga9bbihO32Ga5aiD6o13K2gL58AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAQPc+A79rR+An15ZOx6avpBVzFVWtj9gr+paaS6yAtl/HIu5AVKZuxUzmKskzQOM3xenTUnTtA55JcKmnn/iYCg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:zxgneOQcVg1KKV9+QJPuhXyXWdXIm2Iblibtm/YNSbY","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYZ+rHmf04iTJEStjmga9bbihO32Ga5aiD6o13K2gL58AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB6v4QUq5L9r072Gdqzgmqi1GtkbI+hznomR544zFffUihrCc1cK9a8mYiyIs6YGLWtCgxaqS7vZx9h1STE0wwI="}
